#: 46190139a5e646daa0727a9aaa80fcb5
msgid "Source Architecture and Module Boundaries"
msgstr "源码架构与模块边界"

#: 348780707bb84a409ae6068252547217
msgid "Status: Accepted"
msgstr ""

#: f77cfd3bb6344e10bd64481048c09a40
msgid "Last reviewed: 2026-08-12"
msgstr ""

#: 6098210f57414806bf66782e5a81c544
msgid "Baseline: `582fc51d`"
msgstr ""

#: 1cf890580aea44588598676c8282e328
msgid "Owner: Jittor core maintainers"
msgstr ""

#: 1e7148941b6c40d98bb8cace06d9ddcd
msgid ""
"Review when: a public module moves, an implementation domain is added, or"
" a runtime resource path changes"
msgstr ""

#: 31d342f74e184ce1b9d49f995f5856d0
msgid ""
"This document defines how Python source is decomposed inside Jittor. "
"Repository, packaging, and runtime-resource ownership is defined by the "
"broader [repository layout decision](repository-layout.md)."
msgstr ""

#: 7117f3d088e04465ad847040d0ac7462
msgid "Principles"
msgstr ""

#: f4fa8c5468f24baca9b272ed6208efce
msgid ""
"**One physical owner.** A public domain is a normal package; it does not "
"have a second private tree containing the real implementation."
msgstr ""

#: 42877add3b1244e7a57f71f3d77f6390
msgid ""
"**Imports follow ownership.** Implementation metadata and tracebacks "
"report the module that owns the code. Re-export modules do not rewrite "
"`__module__` recursively."
msgstr ""

#: d597cad7fdf44e71b86fe4525a4d24b2
msgid ""
"**Composition stays shallow.** A package `__init__.py` composes and "
"exports public names. Large implementations live in meaningful child "
"modules."
msgstr ""

#: 05a88e8810984baeb4857f1a2be39ea3
msgid ""
"**Runtime paths are contracts.** Compiler-loaded C++/CUDA resources move "
"only with an explicit compiler and packaging migration."
msgstr ""

#: 6133cbca33c140cb8bda8330b788c180
msgid ""
"**Compatibility is layered.** Native framework capability, reusable "
"compatibility mechanisms, import shims, and downstream integrations have "
"distinct owners."
msgstr ""

#: d756b0d34adf4ff3a619a96cd33eec1c
msgid ""
"**Every move preserves behavior.** Refactors retain public names, "
"callable identity where promised, pickling behavior where supported, "
"backend dispatch, and focused regression coverage."
msgstr ""

#: c560c2c46de644e99289998e7d364889
msgid "Current domains"
msgstr ""

#: b1128b390b9c42d3a2cb9610bd45eebe
msgid "Package composition contracts"
msgstr ""

#: dc9694dd71b14818ac8f2f7080c85e84
msgid "Neural network API"
msgstr ""

#: 9b5314e42b4f40b68f5688db182c3608
msgid ""
"`jittor.nn` is the public package. Stateful layers live under "
"`nn.modules`, stateless operations under `nn.functional`, and optional "
"accelerated paths under `nn.backends`. A public re-export must point at "
"the canonical implementation object; wrappers are justified only when "
"they enforce a real API contract."
msgstr ""

#: 4601ed6aedba402fa6573475b6c49b87
msgid "Dependency direction is:"
msgstr ""

#: 3070c0ea04e843e9baa60312e7a49d94
msgid ""
"Functional modules must not import stateful layer implementations. "
"Backend adapters must remain optional and fail with an actionable "
"capability error when their toolchain is unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: 88f5ab8a730a4f96b1277b8dca22e0a8
msgid "Miscellaneous and pooling APIs"
msgstr ""

#: 8badac134bec4380a78b5bb62eeaf40d
msgid ""
"`jittor.misc` groups tensor, shape, and composition operations. "
"`jittor.pool` owns pooling functions and modules. New code is placed by "
"semantic ownership, not by the size of the destination file. Circular "
"imports are resolved by narrowing dependencies or moving shared "
"primitives to the lower-level owner, not through mutable proxy objects."
msgstr ""

#: e7d594a99fce4e6e8f6c8ecc0a54a8fb
msgid "Compatibility APIs"
msgstr ""

#: 29cc4d4eb315444c9ed952c8dbe9af3a
msgid ""
"The canonical Torch-style implementation is `jittor.compat.torch`. The "
"legacy attribute/module spelling `jittor.torch_compat` is an alias "
"created during Jittor initialization; it is not a second source file. "
"Likewise, the canonical Triton implementation is `jittor.compat.triton`, "
"with `jittor.triton_shim` retained as an object-identity alias."
msgstr ""

#: 19773e31b1344586bc153f3efc3646eb
msgid ""
"`jittor.compat.shim` owns the runtime and deployment code for the "
"optional top-level `torch` surface used by applications that import Torch"
" directly. The name `jittor.torch_shim` is retained only as a same-object"
" legacy alias. The shim delegates Torch-style semantics to "
"`jittor.compat.torch`; neither the alias nor the deployed package owns a "
"second implementation."
msgstr ""

#: b055ed0808bc4e25944fed98916bcf98
msgid "The ownership order is:"
msgstr ""

#: b70d01a2f71e4a1299b74076e98f7c75
msgid "native Jittor semantics and broadly useful operations;"
msgstr ""

#: c8a09e41f1234e9294805a0c86da9eed
msgid "reusable mechanisms in `jittor.compat`;"
msgstr ""

#: 6d3dbfb6328c4813915a1cf6160e1f6b
msgid "optional import/deployment shims;"
msgstr ""

#: 59bf78de5d824bb2af925c7ef855e9ee
msgid "project-specific integrations outside the core distribution."
msgstr ""

#: 869553258f2b4537b4cc850606284408
msgid ""
"See [Torch compatibility principles](torch-compatibility-principles.md) "
"for the behavioral decision rules."
msgstr ""

#: 1d938132147d4bcca25c31890450c2ee
msgid "Import and initialization rules"
msgstr ""

#: 1ae02c6351ed4f5aa1791bb1056d4b23
msgid ""
"Module imports must not compile kernels, download assets, mutate the "
"source checkout, or silently install external packages."
msgstr ""

#: a15250a2404348dea854a6572a3f6f71
msgid ""
"Registration is idempotent. Re-importing a compatibility module must not "
"wrap the same callable twice or create a second module object."
msgstr ""

#: 13edf30829ae4723a21d5b59791ed372
msgid ""
"Optional dependency checks happen at the operation boundary unless "
"import-time discovery is itself the API."
msgstr ""

#: 4bd60e153feb4aaca309ef1fe07eea31
msgid ""
"Broad exception handlers may annotate and re-raise a failure; they must "
"not convert a partially installed compatibility surface into apparent "
"success."
msgstr ""

#: 8dd788af62ee44c4867856392ab590b3
msgid "Expensive imports stay out of collection-only structure tests."
msgstr ""

#: ba104d355f0d4b1aa335fba7558ed272
msgid "Runtime resources"
msgstr ""

#: dfb23d3c330945e7b293a2ff352f2fb7
msgid ""
"The following trees are consumed by compiler or packaging code using "
"physical paths and therefore require special review:"
msgstr ""

#: 0b39c74c712041c5b47c58566d7c2180
msgid "`python/jittor/src/`"
msgstr ""

#: 97991dded45d42258047be3de85e0831
msgid "`python/jittor/extern/`"
msgstr ""

#: 1ad37f604f7b4dc89e592b1b0772aee3
msgid "`python/jittor/math_util/src/`"
msgstr ""

#: 937dc7356eb14efe81c8d62c61f15e23
msgid "`python/jittor/utils/data.gz`"
msgstr ""

#: 4f9cd3e0884e4a65917ddcdd2da2d9ac
msgid "`python/jittor/compat/shim/cpp_extension/`"
msgstr ""

#: af401d0e7a6d4c8ca5532945b5bf9c72
msgid ""
"A move is complete only when source checkouts, sdists, wheels, cold JIT "
"builds, and installed smoke tests all agree. Directory aesthetics alone "
"are not a reason to relocate these resources."
msgstr ""

#: 4f33f2a26c5c487bb552769ae642d7a9
msgid "Refactor protocol"
msgstr ""

#: f7e7cb597aad4ca99afcc78d214aa797
msgid "For each module move:"
msgstr ""

#: 8bc8a247e0e24e4aacd583f74d0f5cde
msgid "Inventory definitions, assignments, imports, registrations, and consumers."
msgstr ""

#: 33feb46010c14cd2948773b9b63eab30
msgid "Define the canonical destination and any compatibility alias explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: 46ea882f3b374043a6a3756cf85e3b27
msgid "Move a coherent domain slice without unrelated behavior changes."
msgstr ""

#: 77264cfb0f044179aaecff55e4021c9f
msgid ""
"Compare the moved definition set and public exports mechanically where "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#: 330a624cadf74c66ad8d0ffa5ef1708f
msgid ""
"Test import identity, public calls, dynamic dispatch, serialization where"
" applicable, and the relevant CPU/accelerator behavior."
msgstr ""

#: f7fb71244b1443c59ab61566fcd48c81
msgid "Delete the transitional source path and add it to the structure gate."
msgstr ""

#: 8430107a398949cca02da5303d1fdcc2
msgid "Update durable documentation and active links in the same change."
msgstr ""

#: 5d8701634161464a88a3e9dcaa6ab748
msgid ""
"Do not preserve two editable implementations after a move. Compatibility "
"must delegate to the canonical object and have an exit condition."
msgstr ""

#: efac2ee05a9640b38581924626af8d19
msgid "Acceptance"
msgstr ""

#: d45c27fe660e49a3b106c33b3faf06b8
msgid "A source-layout change is acceptable when:"
msgstr ""

#: 935ae2a4835d41aca62f411a7d51959c
msgid "imports and public names retain their documented behavior;"
msgstr ""

#: ba0ce8781e7a4f2584735e969bfc7dd2
msgid "no legacy implementation tree or root-level compatibility file remains;"
msgstr ""

#: 88fb1cdac89646858bc86153135483a2
msgid ""
"the wheel contains every required runtime resource and excludes "
"repository-only tests/tools;"
msgstr ""

#: cbddb7af7e664aa49f16dc55f985220c
msgid "`bash agent/scripts/check_repo_layout.sh` passes;"
msgstr ""

#: ef336585bd5b418fa0277935c3124142
msgid "focused tests, structure tests, and every affected backend gate pass;"
msgstr ""

#: 5fb9d2f3638f4cddbe5011692fd1923f
msgid "any deliberate incompatibility is documented in release notes."
msgstr ""
